    "notes": "1. 'Cash and cash equivalents' is composed of 'Bank balances and cash' and 'Term deposits and highly liquid investments (within three months)' as per Note 32. 'Restricted cash' is excluded as it is not available for general use.\n2. 'Short_term_market_securities' includes current portions of 'Financial assets at fair value through profit or loss' and 'Financial assets at fair value through other comprehensive income', as these represent liquid, unrestricted investments intended for short-term trading or sale. Non-current portions are excluded.\n3. 'Total_accounts_receivable' is taken directly from the balance sheet line item.\n4. 'Total_current_liabilities' is the sum of all items listed under the 'Current liabilities' section.\n5. 'Total_debt_short_term_and_long_term' includes all 'Borrowings' and 'Notes payable' (both current and non-current portions), as these represent the company's debt obligations. This aligns with the 'Total debts' calculation in the supplementary table (Note 4.2).\n6. 'Total_equity' is the sum of 'Total equity attributable to equity holders' and 'Non-controlling interests'.\n7. 'Total_assets' is taken directly from the balance sheet line item.\n8. Scale is 1,000,000 (millions) as indicated by '(RMB in Millions)'.\n9. Currency is Chinese Yuan (CNY).\n10. Numbers in parentheses (e.g., for Treasury shares) are treated as negative values in the source but are presented as positive numbers in the extraction as they are part of equity components that reduce the total. The final 'Total equity attributable to equity holders' is the net figure used.",
